   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of supported projects on sustainable tourism development 
2. A network established between the partners of the supported projects in order to share experience and knowledge and develop new projects.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2013">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1- A number of local initiatives on sustainable tourism across Turkey, with limited access to funding opportunities and knowledge
2- Loose network of sustainable tourism initiatives, no systematic exchange of knowledge and experience</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target: 1 project has been supported.
Target: 1 sustainable tourism destination supported.
Target: 6 NGOs, 1 university and 5 local authorities have been supported.
Target: 10 women/youth created employment opportunities.
Target: 65 people received capacity building trainings.
Target: 1 alternative tourism route is created.
Target: 15 women received mentoring support.
Target: 150 people received capacity building trainings related to responsible tourist, disaster resilience and other topic</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 sustainable tourism destination was supported (Mugla). 
33 people received capacity building trainings related to responsible tourist, disaster resilience and other topic.
1 alternative tourism route was created.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Additional 3 sustainable tourism projects selected
Additional 3 supported sustainable tourism projects for 2020/2021 implementation 
Additional 10 supported NGOs, universities, local authorities through grant projects
Additional 20 employed women through grant projects
Additional 20 institutions that raised awareness on sustainable tourism through capacity building trainings
At least 50% of the participants will be women that received capacity building trainings related to sustainable tourism</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 sustainable tourism projects were selected to be implemented in 2020.
3 community based sustainable tourism destinations were supported which are Koycegiz- Mugla, Kars, Ayancik-Sinop.
Additional 3 NGOs, 3 universities, 4 local authorities were supported through grant projects.
Additional 30 women employed through grant projects (15 women in Sinop, 15 women in Koycegiz)
Additional 19 institutions benefitted from capacity building trainings (3 NGOs, 3 universities, 4 local authorities, 9 private institutions)
Additional 125 people benefitted from capacity building trainings where 60 were women.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Action: Financial and Technical monitoring and evaluation of the selected grant projects.
Action: Continuous feed into Webinars, Videos, E-Newsletter, Press Bulletins, Press Trips, Newspapers and Magazines in line with sustainable tourism
Action: Provide support to organization of experience sharing activities (e.g site visits) 
Action: Scalability and replicability studies and development of knowledge management tools on community based sustainable tourism development
Action: Capacity development/training programs for local stakeholders, NGOs, universities and local authorities
Action: Needs assessment of the previously supported projects and provision of consultancy, equipment, etc.
Action: Monitoring sustainable tourism development actions in project destinations with respect to defined indicators and SDGs.
Action: Work in cooperation with T&#xdc;RSAB within the scope of MoU between UNDP and T&#xdc;RSAB.
Action: Develop a cooperation with Turkey Tourism Promotion and Development Agency 
Action: Carry on an assessment to continue either with grant projects or with a regional and multi-year approach for 2021 implementation.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
